## Dosage guidance

Window frame profile: 4–6 phr TiO2. Siding / cladding: 3–5 phr. Fence boards: 4–6 phr. The dosage range optimizes between cost (TiO2 is the most expensive PVC additive) and durability (higher loading extends service life).

## Dispersion / processing notes

PVC compounding is done in high-intensity mixers (Banbury or modern continuous compounders) at 180–200°C. TiO2 is added with the PVC resin and stabilizer; output is sheeted and pelletized or fed direct to extruder. Compound thermal stability must be verified at each TiO2 batch.
